  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Monitoring and Protection of Reintroduced Orangutans in the Batikap Hill Conservation Forest, Central Kalimantan, Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to support successful reintroduction of rescued orangutans into well-protected natural forest in synergy with local community engagement and support, thus creating a long-lasting legacy for nature conservation and poverty eradication. This will be done by: 1) undertaking daily post-release monitoring of released orangutans and providing on-site veterinary support; 2) undertaking weekly project socialization visits to people staying or working in the release area and monthly socializations in the target villages; 3) developing, socializing and ratifying a human-orangutan conflict mitigation plan; 4) developing an environmental education program for school children in the target villages; 5) assisting the villages to implement their community development plan; and 6) developing and implementing a regular conservation patrol plan in partnership with local government.</narrative>
  </description>
